by Jean85 at 2026-05-12T06:41:56Z

> If using this option is needed for upgrading to RabbitMQ 4, shouldn't this be the default? Asking while I'm not into the topic :)

It may be disruptive to anyone already using it, because it changes the name of delayed queues; if your setup has anything name-based (rules, routing, external metrics, external autoscalers, etc) it could break it. It would definitively be a good default for the next major for sure.

Also, it's a requirement for quorum queues, but those are needed for their HA properties; classic queues are still available, they just lost their HA capabilities in RabbitMQ 4.x. So, I would expect all enterprise-like environment to have done the change, but not all of the users.
